{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794292757,"nonce":"6b/8zgc7tsfB4MJHGpX7hUrqPYk=","title":"pointer_events_none on a div does not let hits through to its descendants' siblings underneath","message":"A div with pointer_events_none is skipped as a hit target, but its descendants (text, rows) are still hit-tested and capture the click. The click then bubbles up the parent chain and never reaches a sibling layer placed beneath the content. event_router.rs hit_test_node returns None for the node itself only when no child was hit.\n\nReproducer (blinc_layout 0.6.0): parent relative div with two children: a click layer (absolute, inset 0, on_click) first, and a content div with pointer_events_none holding a title text and a footer row. Click the centre of the parent: with only a text child the layer gets the click; once the content has a footer row with children, the click lands on the footer row or text and the layer never runs.\n\nExpected: pointer_events_none applies to the whole subtree (as CSS pointer-events does through inheritance), or there is a way to set it for a subtree.\n\nWorkaround in the caller: put the click layer above the content and the buttons after it as siblings.\n\nStand: waits for the Blinc team / fork; no change made here.","files":null}]}